    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All green \u2014 full suite: **42 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp29Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, city-region-validated `postcode` for owners, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Validation logic** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/OwnerPostcode.java` (new helper, mirroring `OwnerEmail`/`OwnerAddress`): when a postcode is present it must match `^[0-9]{4}$`; the city's region is derived via the existing `Locality` util, and if the region is known (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) the postcode must be in range. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit value. Null/blank is skipped (optional). Failures throw the new checked `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` \u2192 400.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` + `InvalidOwnerPostcodeExceptionHandler` (returns `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`, 400) + escalation YAML \u2014 following the existing telephone/email pattern.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST pipeline) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT pipeline) now call `OwnerPostcode.validate(...)`.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT) copies `postcode` onto the entity.\n\n**Storage & return:**\n- `Owner` entity: `postcode` field + `@Column` + getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name on both `toOwner`/`toOwnerDto`.\n- `openapi.yml`: added optional `postcode` to `OwnerFields` (so the generated DTO carries it in and out).\n- `postcode` column added to all four schema dialects; positional seed inserts in `hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql` updated with a `NULL` postcode (h2/postgres already use explicit column lists).\n\nOne judgment call: I applied the same validation to the `PUT /owners/{ownerId}` path (not just `POST`) so the field behaves consistently across both write endpoints, since both bind `OwnerFieldsDto`. The tests only exercise `POST`, but this keeps the contract coherent.",
